Q: Why is vector&lt;int&gt; const not the same type as vector&lt;const int&gt; const? A: <p>Simple argument: If it existed, it should be possible to add a <code>const int</code> to <code>std::vector&lt;const int&gt;</code> since the vector itself isn't <code>const</code>. IOW,</p>
<pre><code>std::vector&lt;const int&gt; foo;
foo.push_back(1);
</code></pre>
<p>would need to be valid. Note that the same argument doesn't hold for <code>std::array&lt;const int, N&gt;</code> because it can't be changed at all. Also note that you could simply change the last element of <code>std::vector&lt;const int&gt;</code> by popping it and adding a new value.</p>

Q: Python 3 - openpyxl - Iterating through column by name A: <p>Based on the answer from Charlie Clark, bit slightly modified:</p>
<pre><code>headers = {}
for row in work_sheet.iter_rows(min_row=1, max_row=1):
    for cell in row:
        headers[cell.value] = cell.column
</code></pre>
<p>And when you need to get the value, you can use:</p>
<pre><code>value = row[headers['column_name']].value
</code></pre>
